---
// Redrawn from Figure 10.1 of the dissertation. The original is a LaTeX figure
// that overflows its text block (the save-file box is clipped at the right
// margin) and is black-on-white, which would glare in dark mode. This version
// carries the same components and data flows using the site's design tokens, so
// it themes with the page and stays crisp at any size.
---

<figure class="arch">
  <svg
    class="arch__svg"
    viewBox="0 0 900 470"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc"
    preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
  >
    <title id="arch-title">Insimul runtime architecture</title>
    <desc id="arch-desc">
      The editor layer supplies world templates as rules and facts to the unified simulation
      engine. The engine evaluates them through the Prolog runtime, writes per-playthrough state
      to the save-file layer, and exchanges narratives, events, and intents with clients over a
      REST, WebSocket, SSE, and gRPC surface. A pluggable LLM provider and speech pipeline attach
      as side components used during conversation.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker id="arw" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="arch__head" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- client surface -->
    <rect x="350" y="8" width="200" height="76" rx="4" class="arch__box" />
    <text class="arch__t" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="450" y="32">REST / WebSocket</tspan>
      <tspan x="450" y="49">SSE / gRPC surface</tspan>
    </text>
    <text class="arch__mono" x="450" y="68" text-anchor="middle">routes.ts</text>

    <!-- editor layer -->
    <rect x="15" y="148" width="200" height="108" rx="4" class="arch__box" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="115" y="176" text-anchor="middle">Editor Layer</text>
    <text class="arch__mono" x="115" y="194" text-anchor="middle">MongoDB</text>
    <text class="arch__s" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="115" y="216">worlds · characters · quests</tspan>
      <tspan x="115" y="232">truths · rules · actions</tspan>
      <tspan x="115" y="248">grammars</tspan>
    </text>

    <!-- engine -->
    <rect x="325" y="170" width="250" height="64" rx="4" class="arch__box arch__box--key" />
    <text class="arch__t arch__t--key" x="450" y="196" text-anchor="middle">Unified Simulation Engine</text>
    <text class="arch__mono arch__mono--key" x="450" y="217" text-anchor="middle">unified-engine.ts</text>

    <!-- save file -->
    <rect x="685" y="148" width="200" height="108" rx="4" class="arch__box" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="785" y="184" text-anchor="middle">Save-File Layer</text>
    <text class="arch__s" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="785" y="208">per-playthrough state</tspan>
      <tspan x="785" y="224">single source of truth</tspan>
    </text>
    <text class="arch__mono" x="785" y="246" text-anchor="middle">save-file.ts</text>

    <!-- prolog runtime -->
    <rect x="325" y="286" width="250" height="72" rx="4" class="arch__box" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="450" y="312" text-anchor="middle">Prolog Runtime</text>
    <text class="arch__s" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="450" y="332">tau-prolog (primary)</tspan>
      <tspan x="450" y="348">SWI-Prolog (server fallback)</tspan>
    </text>

    <!-- side components -->
    <rect x="70" y="398" width="200" height="62" rx="4" class="arch__box arch__box--soft" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="170" y="424" text-anchor="middle">LLM Provider</text>
    <text class="arch__s" x="170" y="444" text-anchor="middle">pluggable · Gemini default</text>

    <rect x="630" y="398" width="200" height="62" rx="4" class="arch__box arch__box--soft" />
    <text class="arch__t" x="730" y="424" text-anchor="middle">Speech Pipeline</text>
    <text class="arch__s" x="730" y="444" text-anchor="middle">STT / TTS / voice WS</text>

    <!-- flows -->
    <!-- Labels stack on two lines: the 110px gap between boxes is narrower than
         either phrase set on one line. -->
    <path d="M215,202 H318" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="266" y="178">templates:</tspan>
      <tspan x="266" y="191">rules, facts</tspan>
    </text>

    <path d="M575,202 H678" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" text-anchor="middle">
      <tspan x="626" y="178">per-playthrough</tspan>
      <tspan x="626" y="191">writes</tspan>
    </text>

    <path d="M408,170 V91" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" x="400" y="140" text-anchor="end">narratives, events</text>

    <path d="M500,91 V163" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <text class="arch__lbl" x="510" y="140" text-anchor="start">intents</text>

    <path d="M450,234 V279" class="arch__line" marker-start="url(#arw)" marker-end="url(#arw)" />

    <path d="M325,330 C255,330 240,360 195,395" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
    <path d="M575,330 C645,330 660,360 705,395" class="arch__line" marker-end="url(#arw)" />
  </svg>

  <figcaption class="arch__cap">
    <span class="arch__credit">Runtime Architecture</span>
    The editor layer holds world templates; the save-file layer holds per-playthrough state; the
    engine consumes rules and facts from the editor, evaluates them through the Prolog runtime, and
    writes session mutations only to the save file.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .arch {
    margin: 2.75rem 0 0;
  }

  .arch__svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.25rem 1rem;
  }

  .arch__box {
    fill: var(--bg-alt);
    stroke: var(--border-strong);
    stroke-width: 1.25;
  }

  .arch__box--key {
    fill: var(--accent-soft);
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 1.75;
  }

  .arch__box--soft {
    fill: none;
    stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  }

  .arch__t {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    fill: var(--text);
  }

  .arch__t--key {
    fill: var(--accent);
  }

  .arch__s {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .arch__mono,
  .arch__lbl {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    fill: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .arch__mono {
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  .arch__mono--key {
    fill: var(--accent);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .arch__lbl {
    font-size: 10.5px;
  }

  .arch__line {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--text-faint);
    stroke-width: 1.4;
  }

  .arch__head {
    fill: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .arch__cap {
    margin-top: 0.65rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .arch__credit {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
